hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1702","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman meaning at-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came with a guest of his, or with guests of his. He said: He remained in the evening with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: When evening came, my mother said to him: You have kept away from your guest or your guests since last night. He said: Have you not given them supper? She said: No. She said: I offered that to him or to them and they refused, or he refused. He said: Abu Bakr became angry and swore not to eat it, and the guest or the guests swore not to eat it until he ate it. Abu Bakr said: If this was from Satan. He said: Then he called for the food and ate and they ate. He said: They would not lift a morsel except that more grew from beneath it. He said: O sister of Banu Firas, what is this? He said: She said: By the delight of my eye, it is now more than it was before we ate. He said: They ate, and he sent some of it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned that he ate from it."
"1703","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Uthman, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr that he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one hundred and thirty. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is there food with any of you? And there was with a man a sa of food or thereabouts, and it was kneaded. Then there came a polytheist man, disheveled and tall, driving sheep. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is it a sale or a gift, or he said: or a present? He said: No, rather a sale. So he bought a sheep from him and it was prepared, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the liver to be roasted. He said: By Allah, there was not one among the one hundred and thirty except that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut for him a portion of its liver; if he was present he gave it to him, and if he was absent he kept it for him. He said: And he made two bowls from it. He said: We all ate and were satisfied, and there remained in the two bowls, so we placed it upon the camel, or as he said."
"1704","Arim and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: He said: I heard my father, Abu Uthman narrated to us that Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr narrated to him that the people of as-Suffah were poor people, and that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, once said: Whoever has the food of two, let him take a third, and Affan said: with three, and whoever has the food of four, let him take a fifth, a sixth, or as he said. And Abu Bakr came with three, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with ten, and Abu Bakr with three. Affan said: with a sixth."
"1705","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr meaning Ibn Dinar, Amr ibn Aws ath-Thaqafi informed him, Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me to take Aishah behind me to at-Tanim and to make her enter ihram for umrah."
"1706","Abdullah ibn Bakr as-Sahmi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Mihran, from Musa ibn Ubayd, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed my Lord has given me seventy thousand of my ummah who will enter Paradise without reckoning. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not ask Him for more? He said: I did ask Him for more, and He gave me with every man seventy thousand. Umar said: Did you not ask Him for more? He said: I did ask Him for more, and He gave me like this, and Abdullah ibn Bakr spread apart his hands before him, and Abdullah said: and he extended his arms, and Abdullah scooped, and Hisham said: And this is from Allah, whose number is not known."
"1707","Yazid narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Musa informed us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Qays ibn Zayd, from the judge of the two cities, and he is Shurayh, and the two cities are Basrah and Kufah, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will call the debtor on the Day of Resurrection and make him stand before Him and say: O My servant, for what did you spend the wealth of people? He will say: O Lord, You know that I did not corrupt it; it only went in drowning or burning or theft or loss in trade. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will call for something and place it in his scale, and his good deeds will outweigh."
"1708","Abdus-Samad narrated to us, Sadaqah narrated to us, Abu Imran narrated to us, Qays ibn Zayd narrated to me, from the judge of the two cities, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah will call the debtor on the Day of Resurrection until he is made to stand before Him, and it will be said: O son of Adam, for what did you take this debt and for what did you waste the rights of people? He will say: O Lord, You know that I took it and did not eat nor drink nor wear nor waste, but there came upon my hands either burning or theft or loss. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: My servant has spoken the truth; I am most entitled to settle for you today. Allah will call for something and place it in the pan of his scale, and his good deeds will outweigh his evil deeds, and he will enter Paradise by the bounty of His mercy."
"1709","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah meaning Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih that his father narrated to him that one who heard Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr informed him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Saddle this she-camel, then take your sister behind you, and when you descend from the hill of at-Tanim, enter ihram and come forth, and that was on the night of departure."
"1710","Dawud ibn Mihran ad-Dabbagh narrated to us, Dawud meaning al-Attar narrated to us, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hafsah daughter of Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr as-Siddiq, from her father that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abdur-Rahman: Take your sister, meaning Aishah, behind you and make her perform umrah from at-Tanim, and when you descend with her from the hill, command her to enter ihram, for it is an accepted umrah."
"1711","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Uthman, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr that he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one hundred and thirty. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is there food with any of you? And there was with a man a sa of food or thereabouts, and it was kneaded. Then there came a polytheist man, disheveled and tall, with sheep driving them. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Is it a sale or a gift, or he said: or a present? He said: No, rather a sale. So he bought a sheep from him and it was prepared, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the liver to be roasted. He said: By Allah, there was not one among the one hundred and thirty except that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut for him a portion of its liver; if he was present he gave it to him, and if he was absent he kept it for him. He said: And he made two bowls from it. He said: We all ate and were satisfied, and there remained in the two bowls, so we carried it upon a camel, or as he said."
"1712","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, Abu Uthman narrated to us that Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr narrated to him that the people of as-Suffah were poor people, and that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, once said: Whoever has the food of two, let him take a third; whoever has the food of four, let him take a fifth, a sixth, or as he said. And Abu Bakr came with three, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with ten, and Abu Bakr with three. He said: It is he and I and my father and my mother, and I do not know whether he said: and my wife, and a servant between our house and the house of Abu Bakr. And Abu Bakr took supper with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then remained until I prayed Isha, then returned and remained until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slept. He came after what Allah willed of the night had passed. His wife said to him: What kept you from your guests, or she said: your guest? He said: Have you not given them supper? She said: They refused until you come; it was offered to them and they overcame them. He said: So I went and hid myself. He said: O Ghunthar, or O Antar, and he rebuked and reviled, and said: Eat, with no enjoyment. And he said: By Allah, I shall never taste it. He said: And the guest swore not to taste it until Abu Bakr tasted it. He said: Abu Bakr said: This is from Satan. He said: Then he called for the food and ate. He said: By Allah, we would not take a morsel except that more grew from beneath it. He said: Until they were satisfied and it became more than it was before that. Abu Bakr looked at it and it was as it was or more. He said to his wife: O sister of Banu Firas, what is this? She said: No, by the delight of my eye, it is now more than it was before that by three times. Abu Bakr ate from it and said: That was only from Satan, meaning his oath. Then he ate a morsel, then carried it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it remained with him by morning. He said: And there was between us and a people a covenant, and the term expired, and we appointed twelve men, with each man people, Allah knows best how many with each man, except that he sent with them and they all ate from it, or as he said."
"1713","Affan narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Abu Uthman narrated to us that Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr narrated to him that the people of as-Suffah were poor people, and that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has the food of two, let him take three, and whoever has the food of four, let him take a fifth, a sixth, or as he said. And Abu Bakr came with three, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with ten. He said: It is he and I and my father and my mother, and I do not know whether he said: my wife, and a servant between our house and the house of Abu Bakr, may Allah Most High be pleased with him."
